WEBVTT

00:01.880 --> 00:04.840
Maria! I've finally finished the refrigerators!

00:04.840 --> 00:06.110
Wow.

00:07.570 --> 00:10.750
Master, it's so chilly inside!

00:10.750 --> 00:13.540
It keeps food cold so it 
doesn't spoil as easily.

00:13.540 --> 00:15.770
Ohh!

00:15.770 --> 00:18.750
Try not to leave them open, if you can.

00:21.320 --> 00:25.850
<i>I synthesized iron, chromium, 
and nickel into their alloy,</i>

00:25.850 --> 00:27.920
<i>stainless steel, and worked 
it into a box shape.</i>

00:28.190 --> 00:30.760
<i>Then I added a magical device 
enchanted with cooling magic.</i>

00:31.380 --> 00:34.410
Mr. Takumi, thank you so much!

00:34.410 --> 00:37.970
Now I can cook with fresh 
ingredients at any time!

00:37.970 --> 00:39.850
Which color would you prefer?

00:39.850 --> 00:42.070
What do you think, Sofia?

00:42.070 --> 00:45.560
I think any of these colors 
would look lovely.

00:45.560 --> 00:47.840
I prefer this color.

00:48.030 --> 00:48.990
Alright.

00:48.990 --> 00:52.510
Then I'll take the others 
over to Papek's office,

00:52.510 --> 00:54.870
because it's time to 
start my next project.

00:54.870 --> 00:57.310
Are you making something new again?

00:57.570 --> 01:00.290
I was thinking of upgrading our equipment.

01:00.290 --> 01:02.030
Our equipment?

01:02.300 --> 01:06.160
I had a thought after we fought 
that Goblin General the other day.

01:06.160 --> 01:09.000
Considering we'll eventually 
be traveling one day,

01:09.270 --> 01:13.330
I think it's better to have 
the best equipment we can.

01:13.330 --> 01:14.490
I see.

01:15.270 --> 01:19.220
My blacksmith level and blacksmithing 
skill level have both gone up.

01:19.570 --> 01:21.690
Our current armor's made from magical steel,

01:22.130 --> 01:26.390
but I'd like to create a new set 
using mythril and adamantite.

01:26.840 --> 01:28.060
What do you think?

01:28.360 --> 01:31.480
If it's necessary to protect you.

01:31.480 --> 01:33.850
I'll leave it up to you, Mr. Takumi.

01:34.110 --> 01:36.450
Should I upgrade, too?

01:36.450 --> 01:38.540
You just evolved the other day.

03:09.980 --> 03:14.960
<b>Episode 5
Shadow of Sidonia</b>

03:09.980 --> 03:14.960
<b>Episode 5
Shadow of Sidonia</b>

03:10.180 --> 03:13.840
Mythril and adamantite are both rare ores.

03:14.530 --> 03:18.040
I'm not even sure if there are any
 blacksmiths who can handle them in Bolton.

03:18.540 --> 03:22.010
I'm sure there are some in the 
dwarves' Kingdom of Nomstahl.

03:22.010 --> 03:23.500
I see.

03:23.500 --> 03:28.320
Well, I'll give you a list of blacksmiths
 living in the outskirts before you leave.

03:28.590 --> 03:30.460
Oh, that being said,

03:30.460 --> 03:33.020
you're an alchemist, right, Takumi?

03:33.020 --> 03:35.430
It might require a lot of mana,

03:35.430 --> 03:37.260
but you might be able to synthesize them.

03:37.260 --> 03:38.730
I could?!

03:38.970 --> 03:43.040
Though it might be faster to 
obtain the ores on your own.

03:43.040 --> 03:45.400
Mine them, huh?

03:46.340 --> 03:50.130
There a city called Horas to the 
northwest of the Kingdom of Barcula.

03:50.130 --> 03:53.540
They have a mine where you can 
extract mythril and adamantite.

03:54.910 --> 03:56.200
Although,

03:56.200 --> 04:00.510
you can't enter the mine if you're not 
a member of the Blacksmith's Guild.

04:01.400 --> 04:04.070
There is a loophole, however.

04:04.070 --> 04:05.090
A loophole?

04:05.630 --> 04:09.700
You can accept a quest to defeat the monsters 
that occasionally appear in the mine shafts.

04:09.700 --> 04:13.300
Then you'd be allowed to
 mine ore while you're inside.

04:13.490 --> 04:17.710
Oh, that'd let me kill two birds with one stone,
 extracting ore and fulfilling my quest quota.

04:17.710 --> 04:19.990
I've got good news for ya, Takumi.

04:20.770 --> 04:22.160
Guild Master.

04:22.160 --> 04:25.990
Didja know that Bolton has been 
runnin' low on Treant wood lately?

04:25.990 --> 04:27.280
Treant wood?

04:27.500 --> 04:32.110
Most of the adventurers are out huntin' 
Black Buffalo 'round this time of the year.

04:32.110 --> 04:35.740
It means fewer people are gathering 
Treant wood and the supply's dwindlin'.

04:35.740 --> 04:38.210
That's actually a big problem.

04:38.210 --> 04:41.700
Those Treants, the wood monsters, 
live in the Forest of Death,

04:41.700 --> 04:44.500
which is along the road to Horas.

04:44.500 --> 04:48.430
In other words, you want me 
to go hunt down some Treants?

04:48.670 --> 04:52.400
You can use space-time magic,

04:52.400 --> 04:54.400
so transportin' them'll 
be a breeze, right?

04:54.640 --> 04:57.560
Takumi, it's <i>three</i> birds with one stone!

04:57.560 --> 04:59.480
V-Very well.

04:59.480 --> 05:02.430
I do make use of Treant wood myself, too.

05:02.430 --> 05:03.750
Good man!

05:03.750 --> 05:05.370
And while you're being good,

05:05.370 --> 05:09.300
there's also a blacksmith who's requested 
a bodyguard for his trip to Horas.

05:09.300 --> 05:10.690
I'd like you to take that on, too.

05:10.690 --> 05:14.110
Just how exploitative is this guild?!

05:14.340 --> 05:16.390
Oh, you finally realized that?

05:16.390 --> 05:19.090
If you'll do that for us, 
I'll promote you to rank D,

05:19.090 --> 05:22.330
and your two lady friends to rank E.

05:22.330 --> 05:25.410
B-But I've never done an 
escort mission before.

05:25.410 --> 05:28.800
What about the three 
Lion Fangs that I met before?

05:28.800 --> 05:30.570
Those guys!

05:30.570 --> 05:34.040
They're out on an expedition 
for a different quest.

05:34.040 --> 05:37.090
How long does it take to reach Horas?

05:37.090 --> 05:39.740
Then you'll do it for us? Good man!

05:40.180 --> 05:42.020
Seven days with an ordinary 
horse-drawn carriage,

05:42.020 --> 05:44.690
or about four days for one 
drawn by a monster horse.

05:44.690 --> 05:47.940
I see. Monster horses 
are a type of monster,

05:47.940 --> 05:51.050
so they can gallop at twice the 
speed of an ordinary horse.

05:51.050 --> 05:52.430
In that case, I'll take a monster horse.

05:52.430 --> 05:56.090
Sorry. We only have ordinary 
horses at the moment.

05:56.090 --> 05:57.030
Huh?

05:57.030 --> 06:00.860
Sorry, we're using them.

06:00.860 --> 06:02.100
Riell!

06:02.100 --> 06:04.580
Hey! I hear you're making 
a name for yourself.

06:04.580 --> 06:06.460
Huh? Riell?

06:06.460 --> 06:07.840
Did you already complete the quest?

06:07.840 --> 06:08.810
That's a bit fast.

06:09.280 --> 06:10.660
Not yet.

06:10.660 --> 06:12.800
We took down a Black Buffalo on the way,

06:12.800 --> 06:14.650
so I carried it back before it could rot.

06:15.250 --> 06:19.060
Yeesh, the advanced species keep 
popping up one after another.

06:19.060 --> 06:20.980
Upcoming escort missions 
are going to be hard.

06:20.980 --> 06:23.430
Though that means the 
rewards will be better, too.

06:23.430 --> 06:25.010
Yeah.

06:25.010 --> 06:29.870
Well, I'll head back out in the morning 
to rejoin Heath and the others.

06:29.870 --> 06:32.780
Riell, would you like to 
stay at my place tonight?

06:32.780 --> 06:34.860
Please use our bath and get some rest.

06:34.860 --> 06:35.960
A bath?!

06:35.960 --> 06:37.330
I'd be glad to have one of those!

06:37.630 --> 06:41.550
I need to stop by somewhere else, 
so I'll tell you where I live,

06:41.550 --> 06:43.030
and you can meet me there.

06:43.030 --> 06:45.810
It's fine! I'll go with you.

06:45.800 --> 06:48.260
<b>Papek Trading Company</b>

06:46.550 --> 06:50.970
Then I'll lend you a 
carriage from our company...

06:50.970 --> 06:52.380
with monster horses.

06:52.380 --> 06:53.930
That's a big help!

06:53.930 --> 06:56.580
In return, if I might ask,

06:56.580 --> 07:01.400
could you wholesale some of 
the ores you mine to us?

07:01.400 --> 07:03.130
That's an easy request.

07:03.590 --> 07:05.300
You're shrewd.

07:05.300 --> 07:06.600
Also...

07:06.600 --> 07:12.730
When you return, please produce 
additional refrigerators!

07:12.730 --> 07:15.300
Please!

07:15.300 --> 07:16.090
Please do!

07:17.490 --> 07:21.050
Please try not to open and 
close it excessively.

07:25.060 --> 07:27.530
<i>Mr. Takumi is late coming home.</i>

07:30.910 --> 07:33.200
<i>I wonder if something happened 
to him while he was out.</i>

07:37.990 --> 07:39.940
<i>I should have gone with him.</i>

07:42.430 --> 07:45.910
I'm sorry for making you come 
along with me when you're tired.

07:45.910 --> 07:47.720
It's nothing.

07:47.720 --> 07:52.030
Though we didn't find any blacksmiths 
who could produce mythril.

07:52.030 --> 07:53.120
Yeah.

07:53.120 --> 07:58.580
We met with all the blacksmiths Hans mentioned,
 aside from the one who was out.

07:58.580 --> 08:01.450
Looks like I'll have to do it myself—

08:02.740 --> 08:04.270
R-Riell?

08:05.090 --> 08:06.740
What incredible hostility!

08:10.300 --> 08:14.060
<i>I don't have the equipment 
I need to fight this person!</i>

08:14.750 --> 08:15.940
We're running!

08:15.940 --> 08:17.320
Huh? Huh?!

08:25.420 --> 08:27.070
R-Riell!

08:27.360 --> 08:28.840
How dare you...

08:28.840 --> 08:30.120
How dare you!

08:30.120 --> 08:33.040
How dare, how dare, how dare, 
how dare you target Takumi!

08:33.040 --> 08:34.830
Hey, Sofia?

08:34.830 --> 08:36.250
You're safe now.

08:36.250 --> 08:38.920
I'll deal with this ruffian here and now!

08:39.510 --> 08:40.900
By cutting him down!

08:41.920 --> 08:43.400
Hold it, hold it!

08:43.400 --> 08:45.340
That's not the case!

08:45.850 --> 08:47.590
I'm so sorry!

08:47.590 --> 08:50.760
Even though I didn't know, I attacked 
one of Mr. Takumi's friends...

08:50.760 --> 08:55.840
It's my fault for not letting 
you know I'd be out late.

08:55.840 --> 08:58.300
I'm sorry!

08:58.300 --> 09:00.460
No, no, it's fine.

09:00.460 --> 09:04.260
Well, there's plenty 
I want to ask Takumi about.

09:07.180 --> 09:08.460
What is this?

09:08.720 --> 09:13.090
Yeah, I needed someone to help 
protect me and handle the house.

09:13.440 --> 09:15.700
Is that you, Riell?!

09:18.350 --> 09:20.650
<i>Maple?!</i> Is that you?!

09:20.650 --> 09:21.590
Wow!

09:21.590 --> 09:22.750
You've gotten all cute!

09:22.750 --> 09:24.390
Do you remember me?

09:24.390 --> 09:25.860
I hate you, Riell.

09:30.120 --> 09:31.530
Must be nice, man.

09:31.530 --> 09:35.080
Surrounded by all these cute, pretty girls.

09:35.460 --> 09:38.170
Both Heath and Bogar are married too.

09:38.170 --> 09:41.630
I'm the only one without even a girlfriend!

09:41.630 --> 09:44.100
They aren't my girlfriends, you know.

09:44.100 --> 09:45.060
They aren't?

09:45.060 --> 09:45.940
In that case...

09:45.940 --> 09:47.340
What do you think of me?

09:47.340 --> 09:50.810
My heart and body already 
belong to Mr. Takumi.

09:51.240 --> 09:52.970
And you, Maria?

09:52.970 --> 09:57.020
I've also decided to live my 
life by Mr. Takumi's side.

09:57.020 --> 10:00.060
Dammit!

10:00.060 --> 10:02.500
Riell, help yourself to the bath!

10:03.450 --> 10:05.770
I'm in agreement with hunting down Treants.

10:07.040 --> 10:08.970
Those are precious materials.

10:08.970 --> 10:12.160
I don't have objections to taking the 
extermination quest in Horas either.

10:12.470 --> 10:14.590
If that's what you've decided, then...

10:14.590 --> 10:16.140
I'll do my best, too!

10:16.140 --> 10:18.630
Then we head out in three days.

10:19.110 --> 10:21.840
<i>Sounds like I'll need to make 
more equipment for us, too.</i>

10:22.950 --> 10:24.340
Be careful!

10:24.740 --> 10:28.070
Give my regards to Heath and Bogar!

10:28.070 --> 10:30.990
Yeah! Thanks for the great bath!

10:32.480 --> 10:35.980
<i>Tungsten carbide... That's hard.</i>

10:32.650 --> 10:35.990
<b>Mana Draining Greatsword</b>

10:32.650 --> 10:35.990
<b><b>Magic Steel + Tungsten Carbide + Cobalt + Titanium Carbide</b></b>

10:32.650 --> 10:35.990
m 0 0 l 340 0 340 2 0 2}

10:35.980 --> 10:40.400
<i>It's good for a weapon, but it's 
too big as it is right now, so...</i>

10:45.880 --> 10:48.330
It's really resisting me.

11:06.600 --> 11:09.230
<b>Mana Draining Sword</b>

11:06.600 --> 11:09.230
<b>A magic sword that absorbs the mana of an opponent cut with its blade. The more mana it drains, the sharper the blade becomes, improving its offensive power.</b>

11:06.600 --> 11:09.230
m 0 0 l 580 0 580 10 0 10}

11:09.610 --> 11:12.090
<i>That took away a lot of my mana,</i>

11:12.540 --> 11:14.260
<i>but it's done.</i>

11:14.260 --> 11:16.190
<i>I'll give one to Sofia.</i>

11:16.940 --> 11:20.900
<b>Three Days Later, Bolton, North Gate</b>

11:18.030 --> 11:20.900
Papek, thank you for the carriage!

11:20.900 --> 11:24.100
Your client is already waiting inside.

11:25.520 --> 11:27.330
I'm Takumi Iruma.

11:27.330 --> 11:30.400
I hope we have a nice trip to Horas.

11:30.400 --> 11:32.400
I'm the Blacksmith, Dgambo.

11:32.400 --> 11:33.540
Nice to meet you.

11:36.710 --> 11:39.960
Maria, you're great at handling horses!

11:39.960 --> 11:41.670
I even took care

11:41.670 --> 11:45.830
of the monster horse nicknamed
"the Angry God" back at the Mulan Company!

11:46.830 --> 11:48.150
Guild Master.

11:48.150 --> 11:50.430
We've received word from the Horas branch.

11:51.150 --> 11:54.670
They say the monsters in the 
Forest of Death have grown more active.

11:55.330 --> 11:58.110
They waited until <i>now</i> to 
share that damn information?

11:58.110 --> 12:01.160
Takumi has already set out.

12:01.420 --> 12:04.870
It's dangerous enough when 
the Treants go berserk.

12:05.700 --> 12:08.390
I just hope they don't run 
into any advanced species.

12:11.270 --> 12:12.780
Is that so?

12:12.780 --> 12:16.080
His Royal Majesty enjoyed the 
toilet you offered as tribute.

12:16.080 --> 12:20.170
Yes, he said he would love to see them 
implemented in the royal capital, too.

12:20.170 --> 12:22.130
I'm glad to hear it.

12:22.130 --> 12:26.500
Bolton's sewage problem is 
steadily being resolved,

12:26.500 --> 12:28.620
and word of that has reached 
the royal capital.

12:28.990 --> 12:32.860
Though I think it's spread a bit <i>too</i> far.

12:33.830 --> 12:36.560
The Holy Empire of Sidonia?

12:37.990 --> 12:42.770
It seems word has reached 
Sidonia sooner than expected,

12:43.300 --> 12:45.940
so they're likely to start speaking up.

12:43.530 --> 12:47.780
<b>Holy Empire of Sidonia
Several Months After Takumi's Departure</b>

12:48.080 --> 12:50.340
That's it, Akira.

12:53.260 --> 12:55.740
Don't go forgetting about me!

12:56.370 --> 12:59.420
You're still not stepping in enough, Yamato!

12:59.420 --> 13:01.850
I know!

13:01.850 --> 13:03.140
Well done!

13:06.590 --> 13:09.560
<b>Champion</b>

13:06.590 --> 13:09.560
<b>National High School
Judo Tournament</b>

13:24.730 --> 13:28.500
Monsters probably won't attack
 this far from the forest.

13:28.930 --> 13:30.040
I'm sorry.

13:30.300 --> 13:33.490
I did set up a simple 
barrier for protection.

13:33.490 --> 13:36.110
Yeah, I heard from the guild.

13:36.490 --> 13:38.910
Go hunt your Treants.

13:40.720 --> 13:42.160
Hey, Sofia...

13:42.500 --> 13:46.000
Is there a way to tell Treants 
apart from ordinary trees?

13:46.830 --> 13:49.150
Treants do disguise themselves 
as ordinary trees,

13:49.560 --> 13:53.570
but if you pay close attention with 
sense magic while looking around,

13:53.570 --> 13:55.240
you should be able to distinguish them.

13:56.160 --> 13:57.250
Over there.

13:57.930 --> 14:00.410
Look at the tree slightly to the right.

14:06.260 --> 14:07.360
That's one?

14:07.360 --> 14:09.310
Yes. It's a Treant.

14:10.480 --> 14:11.760
Alright.

14:21.960 --> 14:24.960
<b>Skill</b>

14:21.960 --> 14:24.960
<b>Axemanship</b>

14:21.960 --> 14:24.960
<b>has Leveled Up</b>

14:21.960 --> 14:24.960
<b>Skill</b>

14:21.960 --> 14:24.960
<b>Logging</b>

14:21.960 --> 14:24.960
<b>has Leveled Up</b>

14:22.810 --> 14:24.630
That was surprisingly quick.

14:24.630 --> 14:26.690
No, we're just getting started.

14:26.690 --> 14:27.230
Huh?

14:27.230 --> 14:28.740
We're surrounded.

14:30.200 --> 14:32.620
It seems they're rather enraged.

14:32.620 --> 14:34.650
There's an incredible number of them!

14:35.070 --> 14:37.350
A huge haul of Treants!

14:37.560 --> 14:40.960
It'd take too long to deal 
with them one at a time.

14:40.960 --> 14:42.380
Let's use magic.

14:42.380 --> 14:43.290
Alright.

14:43.290 --> 14:44.950
Wind Cutter!

14:52.410 --> 14:53.660
<b>Skill</b>

14:52.410 --> 14:53.660
<b>Swordsmanship</b>

14:52.410 --> 14:53.660
<b>has Leveled Up</b>

14:53.660 --> 14:54.830
<b>Job</b>

14:53.660 --> 14:54.830
<b>Spellsword</b>

14:53.660 --> 14:54.830
<b>has Leveled Up</b>

14:55.120 --> 14:56.290
<b>Job</b>

14:55.120 --> 14:56.290
<b>Mage</b>

14:55.120 --> 14:56.290
<b>has Leveled Up</b>

14:57.240 --> 14:58.250
What's <i>that?!</i>

15:00.270 --> 15:01.960
An Elder Treant!

15:02.880 --> 15:04.420
<b>Sprite Magic</b>

15:11.840 --> 15:12.750
<i>Decomposition!</i>

15:17.330 --> 15:18.690
It's regenerating?!

15:19.550 --> 15:20.890
Mr. Takumi!

15:21.290 --> 15:23.200
It's regenerating quickly!

15:23.200 --> 15:25.830
We'll have to defeat the 
main body in one go!

15:26.100 --> 15:28.530
Please wreathe your sword in fire magic!

15:28.530 --> 15:29.540
All right!

15:36.640 --> 15:37.660
Now!

15:46.840 --> 15:48.550
<b>Job</b>

15:46.840 --> 15:48.550
<b>Spellsword</b>

15:46.840 --> 15:48.550
<b>has Leveled Up</b>

15:46.840 --> 15:48.550
<b>Job</b>

15:46.840 --> 15:48.550
<b>Mage</b>

15:46.840 --> 15:48.550
<b>has Leveled Up</b>

15:46.840 --> 15:48.550
<b>Skill</b>

15:46.840 --> 15:48.550
<b>Magic Combat</b>

15:46.840 --> 15:48.550
<b>has Leveled Up</b>

15:46.840 --> 15:48.550
<b>Skill</b>

15:46.840 --> 15:48.550
<b>Axemanship</b>

15:46.840 --> 15:48.550
<b>has Leveled Up</b>

15:48.980 --> 15:50.170
Phew.

15:51.800 --> 15:54.430
So Treants do bear fruit, huh?

15:54.430 --> 15:56.400
Those are Miracle Apples.

15:56.880 --> 15:59.740
They're so rare that you 
hardly ever get to eat one!

15:59.740 --> 16:02.090
Then let's take them all home with us!

16:02.090 --> 16:04.410
Should I make us an apple pie?

16:04.410 --> 16:05.480
Yay!

16:05.480 --> 16:09.190
<b>Horas</b>

16:06.600 --> 16:09.180
<i>We safely finished hunting the Treants,</i>

16:09.500 --> 16:13.150
<i>and we arrived at the mining town 
of Horas the next day.</i>

16:14.580 --> 16:18.750
<i>We used our ride to head to the
 Horas branch of the Adventurer's Guild.</i>

16:19.650 --> 16:22.070
Exterminate Iron Moles?

16:22.070 --> 16:23.410
Yeah.

16:23.410 --> 16:27.130
Monsters that feed on ores are 
the worst enemies of a mine.

16:27.130 --> 16:29.660
If you accept the quest 
to exterminate them...

16:30.430 --> 16:33.010
then you can enter the mine.

16:43.910 --> 16:46.360
That's mythril ore.

16:46.780 --> 16:49.900
Oh? That's adamantite.

16:49.900 --> 16:52.420
Huh?! This is?!

16:52.420 --> 16:54.520
We've gotten lucky!

16:54.520 --> 16:55.580
Master!

16:55.580 --> 16:57.000
Something's coming.

16:57.000 --> 16:58.430
From the ground?

16:58.700 --> 17:00.670
It's the Iron Moles!

17:08.450 --> 17:09.240
Maria!

17:09.240 --> 17:10.000
Yes!

17:10.000 --> 17:11.000
Light!

17:15.320 --> 17:17.610
Sofia, can you finish it off?

17:17.610 --> 17:18.320
Yes.

17:19.470 --> 17:22.750
Takumi, what are you doing?

17:23.110 --> 17:25.640
How did you defeat the moles?

17:25.640 --> 17:29.040
Well, they're monsters that 
live in constant darkness,

17:29.040 --> 17:31.290
so I figured they wouldn't like the light.

17:31.290 --> 17:33.290
Huh? That's it?

17:33.290 --> 17:34.270
Yeah.

17:35.080 --> 17:39.780
Mr. Takumi, are you sure it's okay 
to defeat those monsters so easily?

17:40.260 --> 17:44.380
Well, did you all want an 
intense battle that badly?

17:44.380 --> 17:48.720
I-I haven't done anything!

17:49.560 --> 17:51.900
I'm just standing here!

17:51.900 --> 17:57.680
I'm like a mole constantly 
holed up in the ground!

17:57.680 --> 17:59.490
No, even lower than that!

17:59.490 --> 18:02.010
Most moles live in the ground.

18:03.150 --> 18:06.940
<i>We were able to mine a huge load 
of ore without interruption,</i>

18:06.940 --> 18:09.170
<i>and then we safely returned to Bolton.</i>

18:10.170 --> 18:13.860
<i>The next day, I went to Dgambo's workshop,</i>

18:13.860 --> 18:19.940
<i>and had him teach me the basics of synthesizing
 and forging mythril and adamantite alloys.</i>

18:22.070 --> 18:29.290
<i>I combined mythril ore, magical iron, salamander
 gallstones, and crushed magical stones.</i>

18:29.940 --> 18:33.890
<i>That imbued the mythril knife 
I forged with a fire element.</i>

18:38.080 --> 18:41.400
<i>I spent many hours and 
many days on the synthesis.</i>

18:41.850 --> 18:44.400
<i>It wasn't as simple as 
working with magical steel.</i>

18:45.530 --> 18:51.700
<i>I decided to to produce armor using 
mythril and adamantite alloys as well.</i>

