20:01.680 --> 20:03.770
Amazing! Amazing!

20:04.210 --> 20:06.580
Watch your surroundings, okay?

20:07.210 --> 20:08.540
Mr. Takumi.

20:08.540 --> 20:09.600
What is it?

20:09.600 --> 20:13.200
If anything were to happen to you,

20:13.200 --> 20:15.320
I would sacrifice my own 
life to protect you.

20:15.500 --> 20:16.310
Huh?

20:16.930 --> 20:18.700
So to that end,

20:18.700 --> 20:21.170
I'd like a strong, sturdy shield,
 if I may request one.

20:21.170 --> 20:22.710
A shield, huh?

20:23.390 --> 20:25.320
Sure, got it.

20:25.710 --> 20:27.050
Thank you so much.

20:27.050 --> 20:29.740
Although, while I appreciate
the sentiment,

20:29.740 --> 20:33.120
I want you to cherish your 
own life first, Sofia.

20:53.210 --> 20:54.460
Takumi.

20:55.520 --> 20:58.480
<b>One Year Later, Holy Empire of Sidonia</b>

20:58.920 --> 21:01.910
Oh, they look gallant.

21:02.600 --> 21:07.870
The Heroes are about to set out 
for the Kingdom of Samandor.

21:08.150 --> 21:12.110
I'm counting on you, Sir Akira, Sir Yamato.

21:12.380 --> 21:15.330
We shall do our utmost

21:15.330 --> 21:17.780
for the sake of this world's peace.

21:20.680 --> 21:25.070
May Anat's Blessing be with you both.

21:29.130 --> 21:31.350
All finished...

21:37.870 --> 21:40.510
I know I was the one who requested it,

21:40.510 --> 21:43.400
but the load on Mr. Takumi 
is becoming too much.

21:45.140 --> 21:47.840
If only he had an assistant who 
could help him in his workshop.

21:49.280 --> 21:53.250
<b>Kingdom of Barcula, Royal Capital, Bakilatos</b>

21:50.760 --> 21:53.250
What did the missive from Sidonia say?

21:53.520 --> 21:56.880
It seems they've heard about 
the purification magic.

21:56.880 --> 21:59.690
They've written, "We look forward 
to hearing the details from you,"

21:59.690 --> 22:01.440
"and seeing you take appropriate measures."

22:01.440 --> 22:04.300
Then will another messenger 
be arriving in a few days?

22:04.960 --> 22:07.930
Their words are polite, but this...

22:07.930 --> 22:09.980
is practically a threat.
